WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.819
Cheer up, spider-fans; Spider-Man's ejection
from the MCU may be short-lived.

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:09.090
According to a new rumor started by YouTuber
TVO, Marvel Studios' parent company Disney

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.190
and Spidey film rights holders Sony Pictures
are back at the bargaining table, trying to

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.630
work out the details of a new deal that would
keep the wall-crawler in the MCU for a long,

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.520
long time.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.990
"YEAAAAAAH!"

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.550
The unconfirmed report says that "inside sources"
at Marvel have given TVO the skinny on new

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.870
negotiations between the two studios, who
recently failed to reach an agreement to extend

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.980
their shared custody arrangement for Spidey.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.230
Again, we stress that this report is completely
unconfirmed, but it would be pretty exciting

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.989
if the rumors are accurate.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:42.089
According to TVO, the new deal being discussed
would involve no fewer than six feature films

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:45.579
starring current Spider-Man actor Tom Holland,
and an option for a seventh.

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:47.729
Who wouldn't want seven more Spider-films?

00:00:47.729 --> 00:00:51.940
One of these as-yet-imaginary features would
serve as a direct sequel to this year's Spider-Man:

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.589
Far From Home, and would conclude the story
of Peter Parker's high school years.

00:00:55.589 --> 00:00:59.610
An additional three solo vehicles would focus
on Parker navigating the ups and downs of

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.530
college life while contending with a growing
array of supervillains.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.040
But wait, there's more.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.130
The other two films proposed in the deal,
according to TVO's anonymous and unconfirmed

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.820
sources, would be the fifth and sixth Avengers
movies, which have not yet been announced

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.829
by Marvel Studios either.

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:17.899
And in true fan-fiction fashion, these sources
also report that the plan is for one of these

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:22.100
team-up flicks to depict Parker meeting up
with one of his oldest allies: Johnny Storm,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.640
the Fantastic Four's Human Torch.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.149
Is it likely that Marvel and Sony have planned
that far ahead, and those plans won't easily

00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:29.149
change?

00:01:29.149 --> 00:01:32.619
Not really, but technically, this meeting
would be possible thanks to Disney's recent

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.890
acquisition of the film and television rights
to the X-Men and Fantastic Four.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.329
As the youngest member of Marvel's First Family,
Johnny Storm was the first hero to offer counsel

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:45.770
to Spidey when the latter was first embarking
on his crime-fighting career, way back in

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.499
The Amazing Spider-Man #3.

00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:51.560
During a speech at Peter's school, Johnny
Storm spoke about the virtues of never giving

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.560
up.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.590
It was a message that hit home with Parker,
who had just suffered his first humiliating

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.900
defeat at the hands of Doctor Octopus.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.679
Inspired by Storm's words, Parker saddled
up for a rematch with Doc Ock - and this time,

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:03.679
he won.

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:07.820
TVO's mysterious sources also offered up one
final tidbit: Marvel has allegedly come back

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.950
to the table with a couple of bargaining chips
that would incentivize Sony to get the deal

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.950
done.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.230
First, the deal would reportedly stipulate
that Disney, who holds the television rights

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:21.030
to Spider-Man, would allow Sony to move forward
with their TV universe based around the wall-crawler

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.060
and his pals.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.120
Chris Miller and Phil Lord, who co-produced
the Oscar-winning animated feature Spider-Man:

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.970
Into the Spider-Verse for Sony Pictures Animation,
have been tasked with developing the slate

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.310
of live-action series, which presumably are
dead in the water until Disney and Sony hammer

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:35.400
out a new deal.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.370
Second, Disney is said to be interested in
integrating Sony's Marvel Characters, which

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.830
include Venom and Morbius the Living Vampire,
into the MCU.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.810
The Tom Hardy-starring Venom was a resounding
commercial success, raking in $856 million

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.920
dollars at the worldwide box office.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.040
Considering that Far From Home recently became
the highest-grossing Spider-Man movie ever,

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.410
and Sony Pictures' best box office performer
of all time, the idea of folding Venom into

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.890
the MCU has to be a tantalizing one.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:04.450
It would virtually guarantee an even more
stellar global take for the Lethal Protector's

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:09.060
second solo vehicle, which could conceivably
feature Spider-Man next time around.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.820
Once again, and we can't say this enough,
this report is in no way confirmed.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.870
But it's not too difficult to imagine that
talks could begin again.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.500
Fingers crossed that TVO's sources aren't
yanking our webs.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:23.300
We'll be here to report on any official announcements
that may come down from Marvel and Sony.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.410
Until then, the biggest question remains:

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.930
"Peter, you’re still with us?”

